{"availability":"available","full":"ItsIgnacioPortal/Hacker-Scoper","name":"Hacker-Scoper","description":"CLI tool for filtering URLs/IPs with automatically-updated Bug Bounty program scope rules.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":80,"forks":10,"created":"2021-11-07T00:44:35Z","updated":"2026-07-03T06:16:46Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["bugbounty","bugcrowd","enumeration","filter","go","golang","hackerone","infosec","pentesting","recon","scopes","security","security-tools","shell","tool","websec","websecurity"],"demo":"https://asciinema.org/a/llZUBG5BC754rA2yy0Gx7EBqg","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.089Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.089Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.089Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.089Z","stars":80,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Hacker-Scoper is a CLI tool programmed in GoLang designed to assist cybersecurity professionals in bug bounty programs. Given a mixed list of targets (URLs/IPs), it can quickly filter them to match the bug-bounty program's scope. The scope can be supplied manually, or it can also be detected automatically by just giving hacker-scoper the name of the targeted company.","This project is developed and maintained by ItsIgnacioPortal."],"features":["Automatic scope detection: Hacker-Scoper maintains an automatically-updated cached database of public program scopes. This means you don't need to manually specify the program scope unless the bug bounty program is…","Easy customization: You can load the scope of any private program into files named .inscope for inscope assets, and .noscope for out-of-scope assets.","Match any asset: Hacker-Scoper works with IPv4, IPv6, and any URL format (including URLs with uncommon schemes, like sql:// or redis://).","Wildcard support: Hacker-Scoper supports wildcards in any part of your domain-name scopes, allowing you to use filters like amzn.example.com and dev..example.com.","Regex support: You can use Regular Expressions (regex) as scopes to filter any assets. All regex scopes must start with ^ and end with $. For example: ^\\w+:\\/\\/db0-9[0-9]\\.mycompany\\.ec2\\.amazonaws\\.com.$"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ItsIgnacioPortal/Hacker-Scoper/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"edfbbce0f3a5e98f81b7e14ff0abbf178555ffb2e146ecdf06857093c8e1e7e7","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.216Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.216Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Hacker-Scoper is a CLI tool programmed in GoLang designed to assist cybersecurity professionals in bug bounty programs. Given a mixed list of targets (URLs/IPs), it can quickly filter them to match the bug-bounty program's scope. The scope can be supplied manually, or it can also be detected automatically by just giving hacker-scoper the name of the targeted company.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ItsIgnacioPortal/Hacker-Scoper/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"edfbbce0f3a5e98f81b7e14ff0abbf178555ffb2e146ecdf06857093c8e1e7e7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ItsIgnacioPortal/Hacker-Scoper/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.217Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-03T06:16:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ItsIgnacioPortal/Hacker-Scoper/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:48.217Z","hash":"edfbbce0f3a5e98f81b7e14ff0abbf178555ffb2e146ecdf06857093c8e1e7e7","originalBytes":10363,"storedBytes":10363,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["hacker-scoper","scopes","file","path","example","scope","company","inscope","any","custom","database","name","program","regex","cidr","firebounty","only","output","set","using","db8","example.com","ips","ipv4","match","ranges","scope.","specify","targets","urls","wildcard","bounty","bug","cat","chain-mode","explicit-level","files","filter","include","int"